Z||000084||Turbo88||12-21-2001||07:09 PM||||Asking what engine combo to run on this forum is like asking which year Fiero is better. You are going to get the dictionary on how's and why's. I would suggest just doing your own research and letting everyone see what you come up with. Then, regardless of what everyone says, design and implement your original plan. This board is an HUGE resource of information but when it comes to "what kind of mod should I do" you are going to get the phone book! You will hear vendors biased to their products telling you what you can do with their kit, you will have all varity of v6 and v8 guys telling you this is exactly how you should do it because this is how I did it. While their application might suit them to a tee, it might not be for you. I would say, just sit down with beer in hand and attempt to picture your end result. Then work backwards from there trying to figure out what set up will get you where you want to be for the budget you have to work with. Take everyone with a grain of salt because of the previously mentioned "Bench factor" here. <P>Consider your skills and resources.<BR>Do you have a shop? Welder? Air Tools? Hand Tools? <BR>What are you engineering abilities? What amount of time do you have to dedicate? How willing are you to spend to maintain that 5500 dollar investment?<P>What ever you decide, good luck with it and keep us posted.||||reg||1
