Z||000101||fieroX||12-25-2001||08:11 PM||||I can understand exactly where you are coming from Archie.  I guess I can say all kinds of crap, but nobody will believe me until it is finished.  Thats reasonable.  I just know my limitations, and this project isnt one of them.  I have met or exceeded all of my goals, I have ever had in my entire life.  I plan to exceed my goals on this project also.  I know you are saying right now, blah blah blah, fine laugh it up, doubt me please, I want criticism, tell me I cant do it, tell me "you are 22 years old, you cant do anything".  Then I will show you before and after pictures of my 73 firebird, I built from a salvaged wreck into a show car, by myself.<BR>I thank everyone for their criticism, I enjoy reading the posts that doubt me, and flame me, it doesnt bother me a bit.  I hope everyone gets a chance to make it to an event this summer that I will be attending.  I would love to meet everyone in person, see everyone elses projects, their accomplishments, and their masterpieces.  I also hope you all will enjoy mine the same.  <BR>Merry Christmas everyone.  see ya all later.||||reg||1
Z||000102||artherd||12-26-2001||12:31 AM||||Good attitude, I'm 21, who says you have to be middle-aged (and buy a corvette off the showroom) to have a nice car?!<P>See you out there!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B> I know you are saying right now, blah blah blah, fine laugh it up, doubt me please, I want criticism, tell me I cant do it, tell me "you are 22 years old, you cant do anything". </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000103||Formula88||12-26-2001||10:42 AM||||Wow, Ben, you're only 21?  Judging by your demeanor, I assumed you'd be older.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>Gotta agree with Archie and WCF (and Ben, et al), you do get what you pay for.  If you save cash by putting in your own labor, fine.  But my time is valuable, so that has to be considered too.  Neither Archie or WCF are cheap if you have them do the work for you.  Quality takes time, and costs money.  <P>FieroX, I can't wait to see your car.  But Archie's got a point.  Until your car is finished, it's all talk.  It's not doubt, just a fact.  Until it exists, it's all theoretical.  It's the same thing as people with V8 or turbo V6 cars saying there car runs this or that, when they've never been to a strip to find out.  Even though they're driving their car, their claims are still just talk.<P>Oh, well.  Enough of that.  Looking forward to seeing some of these cars when they're finished!  I'm always looking for ideas on what to do next to my car!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000104||80's BOY||12-26-2001||01:23 PM||||good attitude, X. i know the feeling. do you know how many people scolded me for cutting the top out of my Fiero?? "oh you're ruining the car" or "it's lost value because it has been modified." those are probably true, but news flash IT'S MY DAMN CAR !! i can do what i want.<P> true, pics say a thousand words but timeslips and dyno charts end all the B.S. when posted. i really need to get some pics of the Targa on here somehow. oh well. good luck to everyone who dreams of their completed projects. enjoy the thought of completion because when it's a reality you only think of more things to modify.||||reg||14
